    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d460">

                <pb facs="0510" n="1188" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1188"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Wood</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 44.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 17, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Recurring to the suggestion contained in
                    your despatch of October 4, 1861, (No. 19,) which was briefly answered in my
                    instruction of the 29th of the same month, I have now the honor to state, that a
                    pair of Colt’s pistols of the finest workmanship, and elaborately ornamented,
                    designed as a present to his Danish Majesty, have been sent to your address,
                    through the minister of the United States at London, who will forward them to
                    you by private hand. It is the President’s wish that this token of his good will
                    shall be presented by you to his Majesty, in such a manner and with such
                    accompanying remarks as you may deem most fitting to the occasion.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bradford R. Wood</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., Copenhagen.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
